# Wiki
- Pages: `Home`, `Doc-` (only what works in `main`), `Epic-`/`Feature-` (in progress), `Plan-` (old format, read-only except «сделано»), `_Sidebar`, `_Footer`. No team rules in the wiki.
- Unprovable `Doc-` claim: move to `Plan-` or drop; unverified: «требует проверки» + issue link.
- Writers: analyst and architect; tester only «Тест-кейсы»; others send text via issue/PR.
- Impersonal (what the system does: «Gateway отвечает 404»), no customer company names, simple example first; public sources (e.g. Tourvisor) may be cited; links to `#81`, `PR #82` welcome. Dates `2026-10-17`, no «Обновлено» line.
- Names Latin `Doc-Название-Через-Дефис.md`, first line `# <русский заголовок>`; links `[текст](Имя-Файла)`; ADR `Doc-ADR-NNN-Название`, numbers never reused.
- `Epic-`/`Feature-` pages from `Epic-Template`/`Feature-Template`, sidebar group «Фичи»; `Plan-` pages in group «Планы (прежний формат)», no new specs there.
- Shipped: `Doc-` (+ ADR), source page marked «сделано» with links. Cancelled: «отменено» with reason. Doc vs code mismatch: fix the wiki if code is right, else open an issue.
- Sidebar updated in the same commit as any new/renamed/deleted page; rename updates all links (external: stub «Страница перенесена: ...»).
- Before push: `git pull --rebase`; sidebar/links checked; `playbook-security.mdc` checks. Commit `документация(вики): ...` with «Зачем»/«Как работает».
